If you want to serve with @?rice{}(jasmine preferred), start your rice prep now.

== Orange prep ==

Whisk @cornflour/cornstarch{1.5%tbsp} and @soy sauce{2%tbsp}(all-purpose or light, but not dark soy) in a #medium bowl{} until lump free. 

Whisk in @orange juice{1%cup}, @Chinese cooking wine{2%tbsp}(can replace with cooking sake), @rice vinegar{2%tbsp}(can sub white vinegar), @white sugar{1/3%cup}, @white sugar{2%tbsp}, and @salt{1/4%tsp} until combined. Set aside.

== Frying the Chicken ==

Mix @chicken thighs{1.2%lbs}(breast works too, cut into 2.5 / 1" pieces) with @soy sauce{2%tbsp}(all-purpose or light, but not dark soy), @?ginger{1/2%tsp}(finely grated), @black pepper{1/8%tsp} and @cornflour/cornstarch{2%tbsp}.

Put @cornflour/cornstarch{3/4%cup} on a plate. Piece by piece, roll the chicken in the cornflour. Then, using your hands as a cup, shake so the excess cornflour falls through your fingers.

Heat @oil{} in #deep fryer{} to 350°F. 

In small batches, deep fry the chicken for ~{3-4%minutes}, until golden brown and crispy.

> When chicken is done, it should begin to float. You may need to shake the pieces a bit if they get stuck to see if they are floating.

Drain chicken on a paper towel lined plate.

Preheat #oven to 200°F and move the chicken there to keep warm.

In a #skillet, sauté @ginger{1%tsp}(finely grated) and @garlic{2%cloves}(minced) until light golden, about ~{30%seconds}.

Give the sauce a whisk (to mix cornflour settled on the base) then pour it in the pan. Simmer for ~{1-2%minutes} until it thickens into a thick, glossy syrup (honey consistency).

Stir in @orange zest{2%tsp}(loosely 1 orange). Toss chicken to mix in.

Transfer to serving plate, garnish with @?green onion{}(finely sliced) and @?sesame seeds{}, and serve immediately.